    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class with both tests) passes. **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. This makes it a settable input field and, via the `Owner` schema's `allOf`, part of the response. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` in the DTOs and serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. The MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps it automatically by name in both directions.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After mapping the incoming DTO to an `Owner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null, before saving.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Schema is loaded from SQL (`ddl-auto=none`), so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed inserts used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke when a column was added. I gave them an explicit column list (matching the style already used by the h2/postgres seed data) so the new nullable column doesn't affect them.\n\nTests were run on the `hsqldb` profile the suite uses; both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` are green.",
